  "result": "I fixed two bugs in `total()` in `src/cart.js`, and `npm test` now passes all 243 tests (2 were failing before). I didn't touch the tests.\n\n1. **Tax was applied before the discount.** The code comment says the discount comes off the pre-tax subtotal, but the code added tax first and then took the discount. Percent discounts hid this because the order doesn't change the result for them. A fixed discount does depend on order, which is why \"fixed discount comes off before tax\" got 90 instead of 88.\n2. **A fixed discount could push the total below zero.** Nothing stopped a discount bigger than the subtotal from going negative, so one test got -14.5 instead of 0. I added a floor at zero.\n\n```js\nconst discounted = Math.max(0, applyDiscount(subtotal, discount));\nreturn round2(applyTax(discounted, taxRate));\n```\n\nI put the zero floor in `cart.js` rather than in `applyDiscount`, because the comment stating that rule is in `total()`.",
